WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.080
So holmium: holmium is a very interesting
element because it has the

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:08.610
highest magnetic moment of any known element
in the periodic table,

00:00:08.610 --> 00:00:13.700
which is very high. This is basically the
strength of the magnetic field

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:19.830
which it’s producing, so it’s got lots
of uses in magnetic materials for

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:21.460
electronics for example.

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:25.019
Yeah it’s because it’s got the greatest
number of unpaired electrons, and

00:00:25.019 --> 00:00:29.160
unpaired electrons is what gives rise to magnetism,
which is why iron

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:31.640
with unpaired electrons is known as a magnet.

